# Build context for the FRONTEND image (context is the repo root).
#
# Everything excluded here is either regenerated inside the image, irrelevant to
# a CRA build, or a secret. Keeping the context small matters: Docker uploads the
# whole context to the daemon before the first instruction runs.
#
# NOTE: nginx.conf is deliberately NOT excluded — the Dockerfile COPYs it.

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Reinstalled by `npm ci` inside the build stage. Also platform-specific: a
# host node_modules can carry native binaries that do not match the image.
node_modules
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Regenerated by `npm run build`. Copying a stale local build in would let it
# shadow the fresh one.
build
coverage

# The backend is a separate image with its own context — none of it belongs in
# the frontend build, and backend/.venv alone is hundreds of megabytes.
backend

# Secrets must never enter an image layer.
.env
.env.*

# Local state and agent scratch
*.db
*.pyc
__pycache__
.agents
.claude
TODO.md
PROJECT.md
ORIGINAL_REQUEST.md
TEST_INFRA.md
TEST_READY.md
